{"type":"standard","title":"Tom Suozzi","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tom Suozzi</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7794276","titles":{"canonical":"Tom_Suozzi","normalized":"Tom Suozzi","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tom Suozzi</span></span>"},"pageid":1846883,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/TomSuozzi118thCongress.jpg/330px-TomSuozzi118thCongress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":414},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/TomSuozzi118thCongress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1129,"height":1418},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374425344","tid":"52790a11-ae40-11f1-a35b-749a868e853d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T00:24:31Z","description":"American politician (born 1962)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Suozzi","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Suozzi?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Suozzi?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tom_Suozzi"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Suozzi","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Tom_Suozzi","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Suozzi?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tom_Suozzi"}},"extract":"Thomas Richard Suozzi is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for New York's 3rd congressional district since 2024 and previously from 2017 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the county executive of Nassau County on Long Island from 2002 to 2009 and served before then as the mayor of Glen Cove for eight years. His district, which is largely suburban, includes northern Nassau County and parts of northeastern Queens.","extract_html":"<p><b>Thomas Richard Suozzi</b> is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for New York's 3rd congressional district since 2024 and previously from 2017 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the county executive of Nassau County on Long Island from 2002 to 2009 and served before then as the mayor of Glen Cove for eight years. His district, which is largely suburban, includes northern Nassau County and parts of northeastern Queens.</p>"}